{"availability":"available","full":"mckinsey/agents-at-scale-ark","name":"agents-at-scale-ark","description":"Provider-agnostic operations for agentic resources. ARK codifies patterns and practices developed across dozens of agentic application projects.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":428,"forks":100,"created":"2025-08-28T15:48:47Z","updated":"2026-10-06T18:01:11Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mckinsey.github.io/agents-at-scale-ark/","topics":["agentic-ai","ai","cloud","devops","kubernetes","productid-20863"],"demo":"https://mckinsey.github.io/agents-at-scale-ark/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:36.992Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:36.992Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:36.992Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:36.992Z","stars":428,"forks":100}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Ark is a declarative toolkit for building and hosting distributed AI agents. By defining what agents should do rather than how they do it, Ark eliminates vendor lock-in and ensures your applications stay adaptable as AI evolves.","Built on Kubernetes, Ark lets you deploy a dev-friendly cluster in minutes or scale agentic workloads across existing infrastructure. Leverage proven patterns for security, monitoring, and RBAC—avoiding bespoke overhead while maintaining a portable, production-ready foundation for your AI projects.","Ark is designed for rapid, democratic development of agentic systems. The entire stack is built on open-source Kubernetes technology designed for running distributed systems. It can run comfortably on a single developer's machine or be deployed into a Kubernetes cluster across multi-cloud and on-prem environments. Developers and operations teams have full visibility into the entire stack, from the highest to the lowest levels."],"features":["Declarative Agents — Define agents as Kubernetes custom resources with prompts, tools, and model references","Provider Agnostic — Swap between OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Azure, or local Ollama without code changes","Multi-Agent Teams — Orchestrate agents with sequential, graph, selector, or round-robin strategies","Tool Integration — Connect agents to HTTP APIs, MCP servers, or other agents as tools","Persistent Memory — Maintain conversation context across sessions with pluggable memory backends"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mckinsey/agents-at-scale-ark/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"958f14fb92184af681d0872f925d5b25dd84058420ba7a596fd695de2f404cd8","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:37.227Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:37.227Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Ark is a declarative toolkit for building and hosting distributed AI agents. By defining what agents should do rather than how they do it, Ark eliminates vendor lock-in and ensures your applications stay adaptable as AI evolves.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mckinsey/agents-at-scale-ark/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Ark is designed for rapid, democratic development of agentic systems. The entire stack is built on open-source Kubernetes technology designed for running distributed systems. It can run comfortably on a single developer's machine or be deployed into a Kubernetes cluster across multi-cloud and on-prem environments. Developers and operations teams have full visibility into the…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mckinsey/agents-at-scale-ark/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"958f14fb92184af681d0872f925d5b25dd84058420ba7a596fd695de2f404cd8","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mckinsey/agents-at-scale-ark/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:37.228Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-06T18:01:11Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mckinsey/agents-at-scale-ark/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:37.228Z","hash":"958f14fb92184af681d0872f9